Subject: [PATCH] xz: restore the single-threaded default

XZ 5.6 switched the default to automatic threading. The additional decoder
buffers can exhaust the virtual-memory commit limit on memory-constrained
NILRT targets during system image installation.

Restore the default used by XZ 5.4.x and older so callers such as tar do not
need to supply thread options. Explicit --threads options still override
the default.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [NILRT memory policy]

Assisted-by: Copilot:GPT-6.1-Sol
Signed-off-by: Chaitanya Vadrevu <chaitanya.vadrevu@emerson.com>

diff --git a/src/xz/hardware.c b/src/xz/hardware.c
--- a/src/xz/hardware.c
+++ b/src/xz/hardware.c
@@ -407,7 +407,6 @@ hardware_init(void)
 
-	// Enable threaded mode by default. xz 5.4.x and older
-	// used single-threaded mode by default.
-	hardware_threads_set(0);
+	// Use the single-threaded default from xz 5.4.x and older.
+	hardware_threads_set(1);
 
 	return;
 }
